# Incident reporting checklist

This draft needs your review. Replace each [[placeholder]] with your evidence.
Conformline helps prepare evidence and does not give legal advice.

## Record when you became aware

When you learn of an actively exploited vulnerability or a severe incident,
record the awareness time, including its time zone.
Use `conformline incident new --type exploited-vulnerability --aware <RFC3339-time> --title "<summary>"`
or select `--type severe-incident`.
Without `--aware`, the proposed current time needs your confirmation.
Use `conformline incident list` and `conformline incident show <id>` to see
current deadlines and the paths to filing drafts.
[[Name the responsible person and escalation contact.]]

## Early warning within 24 hours

For an exploited vulnerability, include Member States where the product is available, where known.
For a severe incident, also say whether unlawful or malicious acts are suspected.
[[Collect the facts available at this stage.]]

## Notification within 72 hours

For an exploited vulnerability, include product information, the exploit and vulnerability,
corrective or mitigating measures, user actions and information sensitivity.
For a severe incident, include its nature, initial assessment, corrective measures,
user actions and sensitivity.
[[Prepare these details and check the live ENISA form.]]

## Final report

For an exploited vulnerability, the deadline is 14 days after a fix or mitigation is available.
Include severity, impact, any known malicious actor and details of the update or measures.
For a severe incident, it is one month after notification.
Include severity, impact, likely threat or root cause, applied and ongoing mitigation.
Use `conformline incident fix-available <id> --at <RFC3339-time>` for an
exploited vulnerability. For a severe incident, recording notification submission
sets the final deadline from the actual filing time; until then the notification
due time is used provisionally.
[[Record the fix availability or notification submission time and supporting facts.]]

## Submit through ENISA

A person submits through ENISA's Single Reporting Platform.
Prepare an EU Login account with multi-factor authentication (MFA).
Check the live form before submitting; Conformline only prepares filing texts.
After filing, use `conformline incident submitted <id> --stage early-warning`
(or `notification` or `final`), with `--at <RFC3339-time>` when recording a past
filing. This records your filing and sends nothing.
[[Record who submits, submission times and references.]]

## Tell affected users

After becoming aware, inform affected users and, where appropriate, all users.
Explain the vulnerability or incident and the measures they can take.
Use structured, machine-readable information where appropriate.
[[Record messages, channels and publication times.]]

## Application dates

Reporting obligations apply from September 11, 2026.
The remaining CRA obligations apply from December 11, 2027.

Requirement: Art. 14(2), 14(4), 14(8), Art. 71.
